    front: 'A worldbuilder has designed a new continent dominated by massive, jagged mountain ranges and deep, shadowed valleys. The climate is generally cold and dry, with frequent, fierce winds. They are considering introducing a large, predatory animal called a "Grimclaw" to this environment. The Grimclaw is envisioned as a solitary hunter, roughly the size of a bear, with powerful forelimbs and keen eyesight. What ecological consideration should the worldbuilder prioritize for the Grimclaw\'s design to ensure it realistically fits the ecosystem?',
    back: 'Establishing a clear food source consisting of several herbivorous prey species that can survive the harsh mountain conditions.. Establishing a clear food source consisting of several herbivorous prey species that can survive the harsh mountain conditions.',
    category: 'World Building',
    pathwayId: 'world-building',
    difficulty: 'intermediate',
    tags: ['world-building', 'worldbuilder', 'designed'],
