    front: 'Why is risk assessment considered an "iterative and ongoing process" rather than a one-time event?',
    back: 'Because the risk landscape is dynamic, with new risks emerging and existing risks evolving over time.. Risk assessment is iterative and ongoing because the risk landscape is constantly changing. New risks can emerge, existing risks can change in likelihood or impact, and the environment in which an organization operates is rarely static. Continuous monitoring and reassessment are therefore essential.',
