    front: 'Which of the following best describes "counterparty risk" in the context of a derivatives contract?',
    back: 'The risk that the other party to the contract fails to fulfill their obligations.. Counterparty risk specifically refers to the risk that the entity on the other side of a financial transaction, such as a derivatives contract, will default on its contractual obligations. This is distinct from market risk (unfavorable price movements) or liquidity risk.',
