    front: 'Which financial risk metric is best suited to measure a bond\'s sensitivity to changes in interest rates?',
    back: 'Duration. Duration is the specific financial metric designed to measure a bond\'s price sensitivity to changes in interest rates. Beta measures systematic equity risk, volatility measures overall price dispersion, and credit spread measures perceived default risk.',
