    front: 'Which of the following was a key innovation developed by the Sumerians?',
    back: 'Cuneiform writing. The Sumerians are credited with developing cuneiform, the world\'s first known writing system, around 3400-3200 BCE. This system of wedge-shaped marks on clay tablets was crucial for record-keeping and communication in their complex city-states.',
    category: 'History & Civilizations',
