    back: 'The mean varies by person and situation; it\'s the right amount for you now, not a fixed midpoint. Aristotle\'s virtue ethics is sophisticated and contextual. The \'mean\' isn\'t mathematical averaging—it\'s situational judgment. The right amount of courage for a soldier in battle differs from a civilian\'s daily courage. The proper generosity depends on your resources and the recipient\'s needs. Virtue requires practical wisdom (phronesis) to judge the appropriate response for each specific context.',
