    front: 'Which statement best describes the primary philosophical difference between Plato and Aristotle?',
    back: 'Plato emphasized a realm of perfect Forms, while Aristotle focused on empirical observation of the physical world.. The core distinction lies in their approach to reality and knowledge. Plato posited a transcendent realm of Forms, accessible through reason, while Aristotle emphasized studying the immanent, physical world through sensory experience and logical deduction.',
