    front: 'According to Aquinas, what is natural law?',
    back: 'The part of God\'s eternal law discoverable by human reason, based on our natural inclinations towards good.. Aquinas defined natural law as the participation of rational creatures in the eternal law. It is the moral order inherent in creation, discoverable through human reason by reflecting on our fundamental inclinations, such as self-preservation, procreation, and the pursuit of truth.',
