    front: 'According to Chartrand and Bargh\'s \'chameleon effect\' research, what happens when you subtly mirror someone\'s body language?',
    back: 'They like you more and rate the interaction as smoother, even without conscious awareness. The chameleon effect research showed that people who were subtly mirrored liked the mimicker significantly more and rated the conversation as smoother and more enjoyable -- all without any conscious awareness that mirroring was occurring. This is a natural bonding mechanism.',
