    back: 'It needs to be immediate, specific, and actionable.. Effective feedback in deliberate practice is characterized by being immediate, specific (informative), and actionable. This allows learners to quickly understand their errors and make precise adjustments to their technique, which is crucial for rapid improvement.',
    category: 'Meta-Learning',
    pathwayId: 'meta-learning',
    difficulty: 'beginner',
