    front: 'Which of the following best describes the primary role of communication for a leader?',
    back: 'To inspire action, build consensus, and shape organizational culture.. While conveying information and managing external relations are aspects of leadership communication, its primary and most impactful role is to inspire action, build consensus, and shape the organizational culture, driving collective effort towards a shared vision.',
    category: 'Leadership',
