    back: 'To iteratively explore cause-and-effect relationships until a root cause is found.. The Five Whys technique is designed to iteratively explore the chain of cause-and-effect relationships by repeatedly asking "Why?" This process helps peel back layers of symptoms to uncover the true, underlying root cause of a problem.',
    category: 'Problem Solving',
    pathwayId: 'problem-solving',
