    front: 'In GTD\'s Organize phase, what is the primary benefit of using context-based next action lists?',
    back: 'It helps you quickly identify what actions you can take given your current location, tools, or resources.. Context-based lists (e.g., @Office, @Calls) allow you to see only the tasks that are relevant and possible to complete in your current situation, minimizing decision fatigue and maximizing efficiency by matching actions to your environment.',
